A sensitivity check on the total forest fallback
NAI of total forest includes the forest not available for wood supply, so using it in place of the NAI of FAWS probably overstates the flow in the countries that need the fallback. The FAWS map gives the share of forest that is available in 2020 for every country. As a sensitivity check, the fallback values are multiplied by that share. The adjusted series is not used in the main results, and it is exported in the summary workbook so that JRC can decide.

faws_area &lt;- readRDS(faws_area_file) |&gt;
  mutate(faws_share = faws_ha / (faws_ha + fnaws_ha))

nai_adjusted &lt;- nai_filled |&gt;
  left_join(faws_area |&gt; select(geo, faws_share), by = "geo") |&gt;
  mutate(
    value_adjusted = if_else(source == "fallback", value * faws_share, value)
  )

nai_adjusted |&gt;
  filter(year %in% years_report) |&gt;
  group_by(year) |&gt;
  summarise(
    `INCA rule` = sum(value) / 1000,
    `Fallback scaled by FAWS share` = sum(value_adjusted) / 1000
  ) |&gt;
  mutate(`Difference (%)` = 100 * (`Fallback scaled by FAWS share` / `INCA rule` - 1)) |&gt;
  rename(Year = year) |&gt;
  show_table(digits = 1)

