Country grid and weights
Each 1 km cell is assigned to a country, and the weights of every country are added once. The sums are reused for every year.

country_ids &lt;- make_country_ids(eu_countries, faws_share)
weight_sums &lt;- country_weight_sums(faws_share, country_ids)

The weights of the 1 km grid can be compared with the exact hectares computed from the 100 m map. The small shortfall comes from cells that fall outside the generalised country polygons, mostly on coasts.

weight_sums |&gt;
  left_join(faws_area, by = "geo") |&gt;
  summarise(
    `FAWS in 1 km weights (Mha)` = sum(weight_sum) * 100 / 1e6,
    `FAWS at 100 m (Mha)` = sum(faws_ha) / 1e6
  ) |&gt;
  show_table(digits = 2)

